From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:48:07 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 54/55] Plutonium: native windows are their threads' server
 tabs

The Apps panel's window stream is Plutonium's own, so only Hydra's web app
could show a native window away from the desktop. Each window tagged with a
thread is now one of its server tabs: the mobile app, T3's desktop app and
any other client list it, stream it through /api/preview-stream, take control
of it and type into it as they do a page. Closing the tab asks the app to
close the window.

Agents' preview tools and the server's browser don't see these tabs, and
Hydra's web app leaves them out: it shows windows as app tabs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
